# `cell init` refuses a plan as lost when a wipe leaves exactly a Phase-2
# quorum of its members intact: the cell looks lost when it is not (#909
# (oracles that do not judge)). Every tail check a lost cell switches off
# is counted at its site, from the sim's own ground truth, so the excuse
# does not fire here and the `cell init` oracles must catch the refusal.
excuse: skip tail: cell lost
expect: red elsewhere
file: crates/lib/paros-machine/src/cell_init.rs
--- find
    if intact.len() < q2 {
--- replace
    if intact.len() < q2 || (intact.len() == q2 && intact.len() < plan.members.len()) {
--- end
